  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1802.16 River corridor",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1802.16 “River corridor” means the river and the larger of:\n\n(a) The land area located within a distance of 1,320 feet of the normal high water mark; or\n\n(b) The landward extent of the 100 year floodplain as designated by the Federal Emergency Management Agency.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1800) #8326, eff 4-21-05; ss by #9330, eff 11-26-08 (from Env-Wq 1802.13); renumbered by #9657 (from Env-Wq 1802.15); ss by #12185, eff 5-25-17",
